SINA_SMART["anat3-neck-triangles"] = {"lecture":"anat3-neck-triangles","title":"The forgotten triangles of the neck","mapStatus":"auto: generated by universal.py from the lecture summary and key points; not human-reviewed","los":[{"id":"anat3-neck-triangles:s0","text":"Describe and explain: The big picture","topic":"The big picture","sec":0,"importance":"standard","highYield":"untested"},{"id":"anat3-neck-triangles:s1","text":"Describe and explain: About this lecture","topic":"About this lecture","sec":1,"importance":"standard","highYield":"untested"},{"id":"anat3-neck-triangles:e0","text":"Sternocleidomastoid divides each side of the neck into the anterior and posterior triangles.","topic":"Anatomic layout","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"untested"},{"id":"anat3-neck-triangles:e1","text":"Anterior triangle: SCM laterally, midline medially, mandible superiorly.","topic":"Anatomic layout","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"untested"},{"id":"anat3-neck-triangles:e2","text":"Posterior triangle: SCM anteromedially, trapezius posterolaterally, clavicle inferiorly.","topic":"Anatomic layout","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"untested"},{"id":"anat3-neck-triangles:e3","text":"Anterior subdivisions: carotid, submandibular and muscular (paired) plus the submental (unpaired).","topic":"Anatomic layout","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"untested"},{"id":"anat3-neck-triangles:e4","text":"Posterior subdivisions: occipital and subclavian (omoclavicular).","topic":"Anatomic layout","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"untested"},{"id":"anat3-neck-triangles:e5","text":"Carotid triangle: omohyoid below, stylohyoid and posterior digastric above, SCM behind. It contains Farabeuf's triangle.","topic":"The carotid triangle and Farabeuf's triangle","sec":3,"importance":"core","highYield":"untested"},{"id":"anat3-neck-triangles:e6","text":"Farabeuf's triangle: internal jugular vein, common facial vein and hypoglossal nerve. Contents: the carotid bifurcation and the jugulodigastric node.","topic":"The carotid triangle and Farabeuf's triangle","sec":3,"importance":"core","highYield":"untested"},{"id":"anat3-neck-triangles:e7","text":"Submandibular triangle: divided by the stylomandibular ligament; main content the submandibular gland; external carotid in the posterior part.","topic":"The submandibular triangle","sec":4,"importance":"core","highYield":"untested"},{"id":"anat3-neck-triangles:e10","text":"Beclard's triangle: greater cornu of hyoid, posterior belly of digastric, posterior border of hyoglossus. Contains the lingual artery and hypoglossal nerve.","topic":"The three forgotten triangles","sec":5,"importance":"core","highYield":"untested"},{"id":"anat3-neck-triangles:e11","text":"These triangles are landmarks for identifying the carotid, ligating the lingual artery and finding the hypoglossal nerve.","topic":"The three forgotten triangles","sec":5,"importance":"core","highYield":"untested"},{"id":"anat3-neck-triangles:e8","text":"Lesser's triangle: hypoglossal nerve, digastric bellies, mylohyoid. Floor: hyoglossus and mylohyoid.","topic":"The three forgotten triangles","sec":5,"importance":"core","highYield":"untested"},{"id":"anat3-neck-triangles:e9","text":"Pirogoff's triangle: hypoglossal nerve, intermediate tendon of digastric, posterior border of mylohyoid. May contain the lingual artery.","topic":"The three forgotten triangles","sec":5,"importance":"core","highYield":"untested"}],"vmap":{},"mlevel":{"pwq4bc":"a","uxe7ub":"a","bbt6gw":"a","1vncq4s":"a","4h0dic":"a","ntwi8w":"a","1rg2btu":"a","8z1ng3":"a","wtgu3f":"a","4w6v8q":"a","1peu2j7":"a","wfk81d":"a","1t1acqx":"a","1vn21fp":"a","1xkig1u":"a","n9rycd":"a","1vr8tfs":"a","1wmd9v0":"a","vtl23j":"a","sr09kw":"a","1w1mzvq":"a","7pplob":"a","77vyqw":"a","1lp33ut":"a"},"mapCounts":{"verified":0,"auto":24,"ambiguous":0,"missing":0},"mrules":[],"items":[],"experimental":[],"status":{},"difficulty":{},"expl":{"anat3-neck-triangles:s0":{"s":0,"u":["The neck is mapped in triangles because a surgeon needs constant landmarks in a small space crowded with vital structures.","Learn the two big triangles first, then their subdivisions, then the four small ones this paper is really about."],"dp":[]},"anat3-neck-triangles:s1":{"s":1,"u":["This one is not a slide deck but a published paper: Forgotten triangles of neck , by Singh, Vashistha, Chaudhary and Kaur, in the Annals of Maxillofacial Surgery (2016).","Its purpose is to add information on the nearly forgotten triangles of surgical importance: Lesser's, Farabeuf's, Pirogoff's and Beclard's triangles."],"dp":[]},"anat3-neck-triangles:e0":{"s":2,"u":["Sternocleidomastoid divides each side of the neck into the anterior and posterior triangles.","One unpaired: submental, below the chin between the anterior bellies of digastric of both sides.","Posterior: Anteromedially the posterior border of sternocleidomastoid; posterolaterally the anterior border of trapezius; inferiorly the clavicle."],"dp":[]},"anat3-neck-triangles:e1":{"s":2,"u":["Anterior triangle: SCM laterally, midline medially, mandible superiorly.","Anterior: Laterally the anterior border of sternocleidomastoid; medially the midline; superiorly the lower border of the mandible."],"dp":[{"h":"Note","t":"SCM splits the neck : anterior triangle (SCM, midline, mandible) and posterior triangle (SCM, trapezius, clavicle)."}]},"anat3-neck-triangles:e2":{"s":2,"u":["Posterior triangle: SCM anteromedially, trapezius posterolaterally, clavicle inferiorly.","Posterior: Anteromedially the posterior border of sternocleidomastoid; posterolaterally the anterior border of trapezius; inferiorly the clavicle."],"dp":[]},"anat3-neck-triangles:e3":{"s":2,"u":["Anterior subdivisions: carotid, submandibular and muscular (paired) plus the submental (unpaired).","Anterior: Three paired: carotid (superior carotid), submandibular (submaxillary or digastric) and muscular (inferior carotid).","One unpaired: submental, below the chin between the anterior bellies of digastric of both sides."],"dp":[{"h":"Note","t":"Anterior triangle subdivisions: carotid, submandibular, muscular (paired) + submental (unpaired). Posterior: occipital and subclavian (omoclavicular) ."}]},"anat3-neck-triangles:e4":{"s":2,"u":["Posterior subdivisions: occipital and subclavian (omoclavicular).","Posterior: Occipital triangle and subclavian (omoclavicular) triangle."],"dp":[]},"anat3-neck-triangles:e5":{"s":3,"u":["Carotid triangle: omohyoid below, stylohyoid and posterior digastric above, SCM behind. It contains Farabeuf's triangle.","It contains the triangle of Farabeuf.","The carotid triangle is bounded below and anteroinferiorly by the superior belly of omohyoid, above by stylohyoid and the posterior belly of digastric, and posteriorly by sternocleidomastoid."],"dp":[{"h":"Note","t":"Carotid triangle : superior belly of omohyoid, posterior belly of digastric (+ stylohyoid), SCM. Holds the carotid bifurcation , IJV and vagus."}]},"anat3-neck-triangles:e6":{"s":3,"u":["Farabeuf's triangle: internal jugular vein, common facial vein and hypoglossal nerve. Contents: the carotid bifurcation and the jugulodigastric node.","Posterior: Internal jugular vein.","Contents: one branch of the common carotid artery, or the carotid bifurcation, and the jugulodigastric lymph node."],"dp":[{"h":"Note","t":"Farabeuf's triangle : IJV (posterior), common facial vein (anteroinferior), hypoglossal nerve (superior). Contents: carotid bifurcation + jugulodigastric node. Used to find the carotid fork."}]},"anat3-neck-triangles:e7":{"s":4,"u":["Submandibular triangle: divided by the stylomandibular ligament; main content the submandibular gland; external carotid in the posterior part.","Anterior part: the submandibular gland, the main content, with the anterior facial vein superficial to it.","It is subdivided into anterior and posterior parts by the stylomandibular ligament ."],"dp":[]},"anat3-neck-triangles:e10":{"s":5,"u":["Beclard's triangle: greater cornu of hyoid, posterior belly of digastric, posterior border of hyoglossus. Contains the lingual artery and hypoglossal nerve.","Beclard, a French anatomist (1785 to 1825); Boundaries = Greater cornu of the hyoid bone inferiorly; posterior belly of digastric superiorly; posterior border of hyoglossus posteriorly, forming its base; Contents and use = Also known as the posterior triangle of the lingual artery.","Contents: the lingual artery and the hypoglossal nerve, sometimes with the arcus raninus, the anastomosis between the right and left end branches of the deep lingual artery."],"dp":[{"h":"Why you ligate the lingual artery in a triangle","t":"Beclard's triangle is called the posterior triangle of the lingual artery for a practical reason. The artery is hard to find because it dives under hyoglossus, so a surgeon needing to tie it off, for example before tongue surgery, uses the hyoid, digastric and hyoglossus as fixed walls to locate it. Pirogoff's triangle is the other approach, where the artery lies under the hyoglossus fibres. Source: the paper's accounts of Beclard's and Pirogoff's triangles."},{"h":"Note","t":"Béclard's triangle contains the lingual artery (posterior to hyoglossus) and XII; the lingual artery runs deep to hyoglossus while the hypoglossal nerve lies superficial to it."}]},"anat3-neck-triangles:e11":{"s":5,"u":["These triangles are landmarks for identifying the carotid, ligating the lingual artery and finding the hypoglossal nerve.","These triangles are reliable and constant landmarks for head and neck surgeons: for identifying the common carotid artery, ligating the lingual artery, identifying the hypoglossal nerve, and recognising the common facial vein.","It helps in ligating the external carotid artery."],"dp":[{"h":"Clinical","t":"Practical uses: find the common carotid (Farabeuf), ligate the lingual artery (Béclard/Pirogoff) in tongue bleeding, and protect XII in submandibular gland surgery."}]},"anat3-neck-triangles:e8":{"s":5,"u":["Lesser's triangle: hypoglossal nerve, digastric bellies, mylohyoid. Floor: hyoglossus and mylohyoid.","Floor: hyoglossus and mylohyoid; Contents and use = Contained within the submandibular triangle.","Lesser's: Named after = Ladislaus Leon Lesser, a German surgeon (1846 to 1925); Boundaries = Hypoglossal nerve superiorly; anterior belly and intermediate tendon of digastric inferiorly; posterior margin of mylohyoid at the intermediate tendon posteriorly."],"dp":[{"h":"Memory aid","t":"The three 'forgotten' triangles sit in the submandibular triangle and all share the hypoglossal nerve or digastric: Lesser's and Pirogoff's (XII above, digastric tendon below, mylohyoid behind) and Béclard's (greater horn of hyoid, posterior digastric, hyoglossus)."}]},"anat3-neck-triangles:e9":{"s":5,"u":["Pirogoff's triangle: hypoglossal nerve, intermediate tendon of digastric, posterior border of mylohyoid. May contain the lingual artery.","Pirogoff's: Named after = Nikolai I Pirogoff, a Russian surgeon and scientist (1810 to 1881); Boundaries = Hypoglossal nerve superiorly; intermediate tendon of digastric inferiorly; posterior border of mylohyoid posteriorly; Contents and use = Considered the posterior continuation of Lesser's triangle.","Lesser's: Named after = Ladislaus Leon Lesser, a German surgeon (1846 to 1925); Boundaries = Hypoglossal nerve superiorly; anterior belly and intermediate tendon of digastric inferiorly; posterior margin of mylohyoid at the intermediate tendon posteriorly."],"dp":[{"h":"Why the hypoglossal nerve keeps appearing","t":"Look at the three forgotten triangles together and one structure is in all of them: the hypoglossal nerve. It forms the base of Farabeuf's triangle, the superior border of both Lesser's and Pirogoff's triangles, and it is a content of Beclard's. That is not a coincidence. The nerve runs a long, superficial course across this region on its way to the tongue, so surgeons use the triangles to find it, and use it in turn to find everything else. Source: the paper's descriptions of all four triangles, read side by side."}]}},"meta":{"pwq4bc":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e0/recall/1"},"uxe7ub":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e0/recall/2"},"bbt6gw":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e2/recall/1"},"1vncq4s":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e3/recall/1"},"4h0dic":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e4/recall/1"},"ntwi8w":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e5/recall/1"},"1rg2btu":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e5/recall/2"},"8z1ng3":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e5/recall/3"},"wtgu3f":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e6/recall/1"},"4w6v8q":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e6/recall/2"},"1peu2j7":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e7/recall/1"},"wfk81d":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e7/recall/2"},"1t1acqx":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e7/recall/3"},"1vn21fp":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:s1/recall/1"},"1xkig1u":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e9/recall/1"},"n9rycd":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e8/recall/1"},"1vr8tfs":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e9/recall/2"},"1wmd9v0":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e10/recall/1"},"vtl23j":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e10/recall/2"},"sr09kw":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e10/recall/3"},"1w1mzvq":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e3/recall/1"},"7pplob":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e6/recall/1"},"77vyqw":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:s0/recall/1"},"1lp33ut":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat3-neck-triangles:e11/recall/1"}},"explRev":"d5ddf66cb440"};
